  "嘴巴打开，嘴唇稍圆": "Open your mouth and round your lips slightly",
  "舌头后部放低": "Lower the back of your tongue",
  "和 /ɔː/ 比，舌位更低、嘴巴更开。": "Keep your tongue lower and your mouth more open than for /ɔː/.",
  "嘴唇围成圆口": "Make a round opening with your lips",
  "舌头后部抬到中间": "Raise the back of your tongue to mid-height",
  "不要只延长 /ɒ/，还要调整舌位。": "Do not just lengthen /ɒ/; adjust the tongue position too.",
  "嘴巴小开，轻轻圆唇": "Open your mouth slightly and gently round your lips",
  "舌头后部抬高，但别绷紧": "Raise the back of your tongue without tensing it",
  "和 /uː/ 比，更放松、舌位稍低。": "Stay more relaxed, with a slightly lower tongue than for /uː/.",
  "嘴唇圆起来，轻轻向前": "Round your lips and move them gently forwards",
  "舌头后部抬高": "Raise the back of your tongue",
  "圆唇不等于用力噘嘴；不要挤紧。": "Round your lips without tightly pursing or squeezing them.",
  "嘴唇放松，下巴打开一点": "Relax your lips and open your jaw a little",
  "舌头中部偏低": "Keep the middle of your tongue fairly low",
  "别读成圆唇的 /ɒ/。": "Do not turn it into the rounded /ɒ/.",
  "嘴唇放松，保持小开口": "Relax your lips with a small opening",
  "舌头保持中间位置": "Keep your tongue in the centre",
  "这里示范英式非卷舌音，不要卷舌。": "This is a non-rhotic British example; do not curl your tongue back.",
  "嘴巴放松，轻轻打开": "Relax your mouth and open it gently",
  "舌头停在中间，别用力": "Let your tongue rest in the middle without effort",
  "常在非重读音节里出现，短而轻。": "Often found in unstressed syllables, short and light.",
  "双唇先合上，再打开": "Close your lips, then open them",
